**Eureka! Bug Found in Drag and Drop with Pinned Cards!**

Okay, so I just hit an `Ambiguous match` error in Capybara, and the error message is screaming at me: two elements are matching a specific CSS selector for a card. Wait a minute... Why are there *two* of these cards? Okay, let's trace this back. I remember earlier when I grepped for `cards/display/preview`... that's it! `app/views/my/pins/_pin.html.erb` renders that preview.

And then it hits me: **Kevin** has pinned two cards, `cards(:shipping)` and `cards(:logo)`, in the pins tray within `#footer_frames`! That's what is going on here.

Now, this is significant. Not only did my generic `find("#article_card_...")` without any scoping find *both* cards, but this is WAY bigger than a simple selector issue. When I'm in `drag_and_drop_test.rb`, scoping the find to `.card-columns` gives me the card on the board.

**EVEN MORE IMPORTANTLY** - Look at this line in `drag_and_drop_controller.js` on line 183!

    if (frameIsLoading) {
      item.remove()
      frame.loaded.then(() => {
        if (!document.getElementById(item.id)) {
          this.#insertItemIntoContainer(item, targetContainer)
          this.#updateColumnProgress(targetContainer)
        }
      })
    }
The issue is `!document.getElementById(item.id)`. Because that card is pinned in the `#footer_frames` Pins tray, `document.getElementById(item.id)` *will* find the pinned card. This means that condition is false, so it'll skip inserting the dragged card into the `targetContainer` on the board!

The fix is right in front of us! It should be `!targetContainer.querySelector(\`#\${CSS.escape(item.id)}\`)`. We need to check for the ID *within* the `targetContainer`, not the entire document!

This test I just wrote using `cards(:shipping)` and `cards(:logo)` just uncovered a real bug with pinned cards.

Now, I also need to go and check `my/pins/_pin.html.erb` and `app/views/my/pins/_tray.html.erb` to make sure the pinned cards in the tray aren't broken, or accidentally draggable!

